From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Restore original aspect and fresh wave point input contracts

Follow MilkDrop2 milkdropfs.cpp:655-656: per-pixel equations receive
inverse aspect factors, matching main-frame inputs. Preserve the TV
shader-canvas pixels/mesh inputs and all original geometry fields.
Follow milkdropfs.cpp:2526-2545,2613-2624: wave points receive fresh
wave-frame time/FPS/frame/progress/audio inputs before wave-frame code.
Do not inherit main-equation writes or subsequent wave-frame writes.
Keep Q/T propagation after wave-frame code and one-evaluation replay.
Only input provenance changes; no pass, vertex, allocation or additional
equation evaluation is introduced.

Original source: milkdrop2 f05b0d8, milkdropfs.cpp SHA256
68749d31bb6b3020ca89b1e7630fd704e58a5de8dd6275c9f5ea005c6586a7d9.

---
